<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sieradz Voivodeship</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1339–1793</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sieradz Voivodeship was a province of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-poland">Kingdom of Poland</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a>, formed after the Duchy of Sieradz was incorporated into the Crown in 1339. Its seat was Sieradz on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warta">Warta</a>, and it included the Wieluń land. Part of the Greater <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> Province, it existed until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-partition-of-poland">Second Partition of Poland</a> in 1793, when it passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sieradz-voivodeship.jpg" alt="Sieradz Voivodeship" width="320" height="295" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sieradz_Voivodship_1975.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
